# Translation bundles are versioned: every locale folder and every namespace
# file in it is tracked, so adding a locale or a namespace is a reviewable
# change.
#
# The previous rule was `i18n/*` with `!i18n/*/reactory.json` to re-include one
# file per locale. That could never work: git does not descend into an ignored
# *directory*, so the re-include was unreachable and every new file under
# `i18n/` had to be `git add -f`-ed. The files already tracked only survive
# because they predate the rule. Ignore the generated artefacts by name
# instead, and let the bundles themselves be tracked.
i18n/**/*.missing.json
i18n/**/*.tmp
i18n/**/*.bak
imports/*
!imports/readme.md
lib/*
!lib/readme.md
logging/*
!logging/readme.md
nginx/*
